#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mutation check of the join in `--query` (tests/conformance/test_join_j3b.py; docs/joins.md sections 10 and 20, slice J3b).

Each mutant is the new code broken in one way: the lexer's dot, the head of a join statement (what makes a statement a join, the second table, the aliases), the qualified column and the
notes of what is wrong with one (written bare, a table that is not one, the second table of a semi join, a condition on the first table in the on), the key equalities and the conditions of the
on, the writing of the flags (the names of the joined row, the escapes of --on, the six texts the plan keeps), the earliest-refusal rule, the surfaces that read the six flags (jxsrc and the
modules of the join), the conflicts, the repairs. A mutant is killed when a test fails or the build refuses it; one that survives is a hole in the gates, or an equivalent mutant, which is
then listed in EQUIVALENT with the reason it changes nothing.

    python3 scripts/query_join_mutants.py [name-substring ...]

`--check` only verifies that every site still matches (no build; CI runs it). See mutlib.py.
"""
import sys

sys.path.insert(0, __import__('os').path.dirname(__import__('os').path.abspath(__file__)))
import mutlib  # noqa: E402

